<main class="home">
    <section class="home-hero">
        <div>
            <h1>Your AI writes it. Parachute shows it to you.</h1>
            <p class="lede">A vault of your own that Claude, ChatGPT or any AI can read and write. The Parachute app shows what is in it: your records, the small screens your AI makes for them, and a home you arrange together.</p>
            <p class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs/use/start/">Get Parachute</a> <a class="plain" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a></p>
        </div>
        <aside class="connect-card" aria-label="Connect your AI">
            <h2>Connect your AI</h2>
            <p>Give it your vault's address:</p>
            <code class="url">https://my.parachute.computer/vault/&lt;your vault&gt;/mcp</code>
            <p>Then ask it:</p>
            <ol>
                <li>Make me a reading tracker I can use in Parachute.</li>
                <li>What did I capture this week? Sort it into the right places.</li>
                <li>Make me a home screen with my journal and my reading list pinned.</li>
            </ol>
            <p style="margin:.8rem 0 0"><a href="/docs/use/connect-your-ai/">Claude, ChatGPT and others, step by step</a></p>
        </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="home-band" aria-labelledby="layers">
        <h2 id="layers">Everything is a record</h2>
        <ol class="layers">
            <li><b>Your vault</b><span>Where it is kept: Parachute Cloud, or a server of your own. Plain markdown you can export.</span><code>https://…/vault/home/mcp</code></li>
            <li><b>Types and records</b><span>A book, a meeting, a recipe: each a record with fields. Your AI makes the types it needs.</span><code>Books/Piranesi · type book</code></li>
            <li><b>Applets</b><span>A small screen, one record of code. It runs only after you allow it, and sees only what its card says.</span><code>Applets/Reading · tagged applet</code></li>
            <li><b>Your home</b><span>A bundle: one record that picks your home, your pins and your applets.</span><code>Parachute/Apps/&lt;id&gt;</code></li>
        </ol>
        <p style="margin-top:1rem"><a href="/docs/build/how-it-works/">One reading tracker, through every layer</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="home-band" aria-labelledby="doors">
        <h2 id="doors">The docs</h2>
        {% include "doors.njk" %}
    </section>

    <section class="home-band" aria-labelledby="yours">
        <h2 id="yours">Yours to keep</h2>
        <p style="max-width:44rem">Open source (AGPL). The same vault engine runs on Parachute Cloud and on your own machine, and a vault moves between them as a file. Your AI works for you on your records; nothing runs that you didn't allow.</p>
